PER-FILE HEADERS

Files authored for this repository carry the short Apache header. Files copied
verbatim from Syntology's working repository -- everything in src/ except the
query_engine stand-in -- deliberately do not: they are byte-identical to the
code that produced the published numbers, and MANIFEST.json records each one's
sha256 so that can be checked. Apache-2.0 does not require a per-file header,
and buying one here would cost the property that makes the tree auditable.
src/PORTABILITY_PATCHES.md lists the 18 files that are not byte-identical and
exactly what was changed in each.

ATTRIBUTION TO THE PAPERS

Each of the 72 tasks names an arXiv paper by identifier and title -- 72
distinct papers, 72 distinct methods -- and describes one of its methods;
referees/INDEX.json is the machine-readable list, and
tasks/*.json carries the same for each task set. That is citation, not
licensed reuse. The attribution string the tools return with any served
implementation is: "Reference implementation attributed to arXiv:<id>;
reference code, not audited production code."

WHAT IS NOT IN THIS REPOSITORY, AND SO IS NOT LICENSED BY IT

- The 118,400-row flat code index. 115,574 rows were harvested from public
  GitHub repositories and 71.0% of those carry no licence that permits
  redistribution (data/corpus/license_census.json).
- Raw transcripts and submitted solutions, for the same reason: they contain
  fetched third-party source. data/runs/**/transcript.json ships the redacted
  form instead -- structure kept, every retrieved body replaced by a digest.
- query_engine, Syntology's production serving package. src/vendor/query_engine
  is a stand-in written for this repository.
- Any snapshot of the Syntology graph.

If a licence-filtered index is ever published, every row in it carries its own
upstream licence and needs its own attribution. Nothing here extends to it.
